    </fieldPermissions>
    <!--
        🔴 Task.WhoId IS NOW DECLARED HERE — DO NOT REMOVE OR RE-HIDE IT IN A COMMENT.
        This block used to say WhoId was "deliberately NOT declared," on the theory that an
        org-side-only grant (created by hand 2026-08-01, read+edit, to unblock the live
        inbound-email pipeline — the Email Service context user, Minimum Access profile, could not
        see Task.WhoId when the pipeline logs an inbound-email Task on a Lead/Contact target) would
        survive a metadata redeploy of this file untouched. It does NOT: a Metadata API deploy of a
        PermissionSet REPLACES its entire field-permission set rather than merging with the org's
        existing rows, so the 2026-08-05 Activity-prefix-casing fix (see the top comment block)
        silently wiped this org-side row along with everything else not declared in-repo, and every
        inbound email routing to a Lead or Contact then failed with `System.DmlException |
        Operation failed due to fields being inaccessible on Sobject Task` — the Task never logged,
        losing both the activity-timeline entry and the `Inbound_Message_Id__c`
        redelivery-idempotency key. Fixed 2026-08-06 by declaring the field below, matching every
        other Task.* row in this file. `DPEG_Task_Edit.permissionset-meta.xml` still does not grant
        Task.WhoId — that is a SEPARATE permission set for a different persona and is out of scope
        here; do not "harmonize" it without a reason specific to that persona.
    -->
